---
source: crates/gamepadii/tests/cli.rs
expression: "help(&[\"restore\"])"
---
Write the config blob of a backup file back to the pad, over the control channel (needs v1.6). This writes all the settings to flash.

gamepadii checks the file and the pad first: the same board, and enough free space. It backs up the config of the pad, sends the blob, and the pad restarts with it. Then gamepadii reads the saved config again and compares its CRC-32.

Usage: gamepadii restore [OPTIONS] <FILE>

Arguments:
  <FILE>
          The backup file (from `backup`), or - for standard input

Options:
      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - human:  Text for people
          - json:   The versioned JSON contract ("schema": 1)
          - waybar: One line of waybar custom-module JSON; `status` and `leds` only
          
          [default: human]

      --no-backup
          Don't back up the config of the pad first

      --json
          Same as `--format json`

      --timeout <SECS>
          How long to wait for the pad on USB after the restart
          
          [default: 10]

      --host <HOST>
          Talk to the web configurator at HOST (host, host:port or http://host) without looking for the pad on USB first. The default is to find it on USB and use 192.168.7.1

      --no-channel
          Don't use the USB control channel (the gamepadii firmware's): only web-config and button presses

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
